-2.1 For the ordered transform, if $A=0$ then $B=0$ and all outputs vanish. Otherwise oddness allows $A>0$. Since $0\le A+B\le2A$ and $2A$ is representable, monotonicity gives $0\le S\le2A$. If $B\ge-A/2$, it also gives $S\ge A/2$; step 1.3 then makes $S-A$ exact. If $B<-A/2$, the operands $A$ and $-B$ meet step 1.3, so $S=A+B$ exactly and $S-A=B$ is exact as well. Thus always $Z=S-A=B+\rho$, where $\rho=S-(A+B)$. Step 1.2 makes $-\rho$ representable, so $T=R(B-Z)=-\rho=A+B-S$ exactly. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 1.3, algebra] ∎
